# Repo roles

Two checkouts share this product. Put the change in the repo that owns that kind of work.

| Work | Repo | Path | Branch |
|------|------|------|--------|
| Servers, Docker, containers, identity, annotation, export, OData, segmentation, section correction, `gRPC_Protos`, and the gRPC clients (the gRPC Viking, Jotunn) | **Viking** | `d:\src\git\Viking` | `dev` |
| WCF clients (Viking, VikingAU, MonogameTestbed, shared client libraries); Viking Test builds are packed from here | **VikingLegacy** | `d:\src\git\VikingLegacy` | `Legacy` |

## Keep clients in parallel

Viking has a `Clients/` tree too: the gRPC client was ported from VikingLegacy's. Keep the two aligned so fixes reach both.

- Land WCF client changes in **VikingLegacy** first.
- Mirror the same change into Viking `Clients/` (and any shared client projects it touches) on a best-effort basis in the same piece of work, where the gRPC client has the same code.
- If a client fix is made in Viking and it affects the WCF client, back port it into VikingLegacy the same way.
- Do not let the two client trees drift when the mirror is practical in the same change.

Server and container changes stay in Viking. VikingLegacy runs no servers; do not start that work there.

```text
WCF Viking annotation fix
  → edit Clients/Viking in VikingLegacy
  → mirror the same edit under Clients/ in Viking

IdentityServer compose / cert change
  → edit Servers/ in Viking only
```
